  "title": "How to Calculate Volume & Surface Area",
  "content": "<p>Key formulas (given on the exam formula sheet for cones/spheres):</p><p>$$\\text{Prism volume} = \\text{cross-section area} \\times \\text{length}$$</p><p>$$\\text{Cylinder: } V = \\pi r^2 h \\qquad \\text{SA} = 2\\pi r^2 + 2\\pi rh$$</p><p>$$\\text{Cone: } V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h \\qquad \\text{Curved SA} = \\pi r l$$</p><p>$$\\text{Sphere: } V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 \\qquad \\text{SA} = 4\\pi r^2$$</p><p>$$\\text{Pyramid: } V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times h$$</p><p>For compound solids, add or subtract the volumes of simpler shapes. Always check units match.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Find the volume of a cylinder with radius 4 cm and height 10 cm.</strong></p><p>\\(V = \\pi \\times 4^2 \\times 10 = 160\\pi \\approx 502.7\\) cm³</p>"
 },
